Fixed. The bug was the case-sensitive URL comparison in `src/import_merge.ts:7`.

**Change:** `b.url === inc.url` → compares normalized URLs via `new URL(url).href`, which lowercases the scheme and host. Case-variant hostnames (`https://example.com/a` vs `https://EXAMPLE.com/a`) now match and merge, keeping the existing entry and unioning tags. Non-URL strings fall back to raw comparison so nothing breaks.

Verified: `deno check` and `deno test` pass (3 tests), and a case-variant import now produces a single entry with unioned tags `["x","y"]`.


